invariant: INV-17
file: sha512_compress_blocks.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha512-stack
reason: SHA512_COMPRESS_BLOCKS_BELOW_LEN, the bytes of stack sha512.c wipes
  below each compression call, is 240. That covers the 200 bytes
  sha512_compress_blocks writes below its caller under gcc 13.3 for
  x86-64 and the 184 to 224 it writes for arm64, so bin/sha2_equiv_test
  passes on every machine's own compiler and in the lane's gcc runs.
  Under clang for x86-64 the function writes 264 bytes, and the wipe
  leaves a word the call computed from its message below it. build.zig
  builds the object with clang. The lane's sha512-stack part builds the
  binary with clang for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64, where it
  measures the 264 bytes against the length and then finds the word. The
  lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than
  caught.

--- old
#define SHA512_COMPRESS_BLOCKS_BELOW_LEN 512
--- new
#define SHA512_COMPRESS_BLOCKS_BELOW_LEN 240
